  "question": {
    "text": "A material ' $B$ ' has twice the specific resistance of ' $A$ '. A circular wire made of ' $B$ ' has twice the diameter of a wire made of ' $A$ '. Then for the two wires to have the same resistance, the ratio $\\ell_A / \\ell_B$ of their respective lengths must be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iYMVY",
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ld4mg",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pWUyo",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oCyr1",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{R}_1=\\frac{\\rho_{\\mathrm{A}} \\ell_{\\mathrm{A}}}{\\pi \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{A}}^2} \\quad \\mathrm{R}_2=\\frac{\\rho_{\\mathrm{B}} \\ell_{\\mathrm{B}}}{\\pi \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{B}}^2}$\n$\\frac{\\ell_{\\mathrm{A}}}{\\ell_{\\mathrm{B}}}=\\frac{\\rho_{\\mathrm{B}} \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{A}}^2}{\\rho_{\\mathrm{A}} \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{B}}^2}=\\frac{2 \\rho_{\\mathrm{A}} \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{A}}^2}{\\rho_{\\mathrm{A}} \\cdot 4 \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{A}}^2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\ell_{\\mathrm{B}}}{\\ell_{\\mathrm{A}}}=2$",
    "image": null
  },
